es is a retirement: it is owed while its recorded copy holds the row and taken once the copy does not; on a held rung it derives no act. A first approval of an absent row is inconsistent and refuses naming the row. Each row's act follows the held-rung policy that also informs the judging brief, with the bless mark as the added condition for a released-rung MEANING row.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_MEANING_BLESS_row_reads_MEANING_and_blessed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_an_unmarked_MEANING_row_is_not_blessed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_row_tagged_both_ways_is_not_blessed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_each_unaccepted_or_unreadable_verdict_is_refused_naming_why; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_mixed_first_approval_verdict_approves_only_its_approved_rows_registries; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_MEANING_row_without_the_bless_mark_is_left_unacted; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_blessed_MEANING_row_on_a_released_rung_is_reattested; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_blessed_MEANING_row_on_a_held_rung_is_left_unacted; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_rung_CLARITY_row_is_reattested_naming_its_verdict; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_held_rung_APPROVE_row_owes_no_act; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_combined_verdict_lists_the_amendment_act_before_the_first_approval_act; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_combined_act_interrupted_between_its_commits_lists_only_the_first_approval_act; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_flip_committed_without_its_copy_is_refused_naming_the_row; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_Drafted_row_present_unchanged_in_a_whole_registry_copy_is_owed; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_reattest_of_a_row_below_Approved_is_refused_naming_the_row; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_a_completed_act_owes_none_and_is_refused; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_the_rendered_act_commands_survive_a_shell; tests/test_adjudicate_act.py::test_the_ac